module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a nullary function's NAME, written where a VALUE of that function's return type is declared, is accepted with no diagnostic. empty_map stands where empty_map() was meant, so the position holds a fn() -> Map<String, Bool> where a Map<String, Bool> is required. ",

    "HARM: the author reads a clean compile as verification of the seam the change introduced. That is the specification-without-execution shape of DESIGN section 5 arriving through the compiler rather than around it, which is worse than the ordinary form because the clean compile is the very artifact the author is entitled to trust. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, AND IT IS WHAT MAKES THIS A GAP RATHER THAN A LIMIT: the refusal is REACHABLE AT THE SAME POSITION IN THE SAME COMPILE. A four-arm fixture declares take_map_concrete(m: Map<String, Bool>). Arm 3 hands that formal a String and the compile REFUSES, located and typed -- type mismatch: expected 'Map(...)', got 'Primitive(String)'. Arm 4 hands that identical formal an unapplied empty_map and the compile is SILENT: 1 blocking error, and it is arm 3's. So the checker decides shape at this position and does not decide THIS shape. ",

    "AND THE MISMATCH IS DECIDABLE WITHOUT DECIDING ANYTHING ELSE. No instantiation of any type variable makes fn() -> T inhabit T, because a function type and its result type are different constructors. The judgment needs the argument's own shape and nothing about the declared position beyond its being a non-function type. ",

    "THIS IS NOT THE GENERIC-FORMAL DEFERRAL AND MUST NOT BE FOLDED INTO IT. Arm 4's position is CONCRETE. The generic-formal population is owned by generic_application_admits_distinct_unit_variant_arguments, whose ceiling sentence this same fixture discharges in a separate receipt there; that row's subject is variant identity at a generic position, and this row's subject is a function value at a concrete one. Two mechanisms, one consequence -- a decidable mismatch admitted -- and folding them would let a repair for either be credited to both. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder. The invalid state is accepted with no diagnostic at all, so nothing is mitigated, and an accepted wrong program is not a rung. CEILING: structurally impossible, and the ceiling is DERIVED rather than aspirational -- the class is decidable from the argument alone, its authority is the same declared-type judgment that already refuses arm 3, and 'undecidable' is not available as an excuse here because the sibling diagnostic's own name has been measured not to be a limit. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the declared-type judgment decides FUNCTION-TYPE-AGAINST-NON-FUNCTION-TYPE from the argument's own shape before it consults the declared position, sufficient that arm 4 refuses with a located, typed mismatch in the same compile in which arm 3 does. Nothing else retires this row. The trigger names that capability rather than the fixture, because a fixture that merely exists would satisfy a fixture-shaped trigger while the capability stayed dead. ",

    "EVIDENCE OBLIGATION ON THE CLIMB: arm 4 is enrolled as the discriminating RED and arm 3 as the accepted positive control, and neither retires when the wall lands -- arm 4 flips from an expecting-accept boundary probe to a permanent refusing regression control. The present acceptance is the defect, not desired language behaviour. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a compile over a change comes back clean, ask whether any argument the change introduced is a bare function name at a position declared as a value. The behavioural tell is that the defect is found by a READER rather than by the compiler, on a diff the compiler reported nothing about.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
